WEBVTT

00:01.539 --> 00:05.057
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.060 --> 00:08.387
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.438 --> 00:11.867
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.934 --> 00:14.827
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.911 --> 00:18.454
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.506 --> 00:21.649
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.734 --> 00:23.272
♪ All the things that make us

00:23.339 --> 00:24.693
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.777 --> 00:30.044
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:37.241 --> 00:39.447
You guys, don't you think
I'm a little old

00:39.516 --> 00:41.872
for the Teen Choice Awards?
I mean, I turned 18 today.

00:41.956 --> 00:43.261
Oh, come on, Meg.

00:43.328 --> 00:45.351
You always used to love
the Teen Choice Awards.

00:45.419 --> 00:47.157
Yeah, ever since Fox
pulled this contrived night

00:47.225 --> 00:49.832
of (bleep) out of
their ass, in an effort

00:49.900 --> 00:51.438
to get in on the awards
show business,

00:51.505 --> 00:53.361
it's been very
special to you.

00:53.412 --> 00:57.709
<i>ANNOUNCER: Coming to you live, it's
the Teen Choice Awards!</i>

00:57.760 --> 00:59.265
Featuring...

00:59.349 --> 01:00.268
(girls scream)

01:01.556 --> 01:02.408
(girls scream)

01:03.563 --> 01:04.415
(girls scream)

01:05.570 --> 01:06.957
(girls scream)

01:07.041 --> 01:09.717
I tell ya, every year, I
recognize fewer and fewer names.

01:11.055 --> 01:11.907
(girls scream)

01:13.179 --> 01:14.064
(girls scream)

01:15.203 --> 01:16.071
(girls scream)

01:17.661 --> 01:22.343
(girls continue to scream
with each announcement)

01:27.310 --> 01:29.282
<i>And a live performance by...</i>

01:32.478 --> 01:36.607
<i>Plus we tally your text vote
for the Biggest Whiff</i>

01:36.675 --> 01:38.246
<i>and Choice Bro-ment
of the Year!</i>

01:49.084 --> 01:50.253
<i>And now your host...</i>

01:50.322 --> 01:52.360
<i>Wavyhair Doucheston!</i>

01:52.411 --> 01:53.414
(girls screaming)

01:55.288 --> 01:57.360
I touched him!

01:57.428 --> 01:59.468
What's up, Teen Choice Awards?!

02:00.924 --> 02:02.394
We're gonna kick things off

02:02.445 --> 02:03.866
with Choice Lacrosse Guy Smile!

02:03.934 --> 02:08.749
Give it up for our first
presenter, Wilford Brimley!

02:08.818 --> 02:11.308
It's entirely too loud in here!

02:11.393 --> 02:13.031
Quiet down!

02:13.098 --> 02:15.271
There's no accountability
anymore!

02:15.339 --> 02:16.609
I have diabetes!

02:16.677 --> 02:19.369
Hey, what do you say we get
some music in here, huh?

02:19.436 --> 02:20.907
No, that'll only
make things worse!

02:20.975 --> 02:23.415
Give it up for our first
nominated Choice Band

02:23.484 --> 02:26.058
of the Night,
Peehole Skin!

02:26.142 --> 02:27.847
(rock music plays)

02:27.898 --> 02:30.071
♪ (grunts) Feelings

02:30.156 --> 02:30.992
(girls scream)

02:31.043 --> 02:33.466
♪ (grunts) Feelings

02:33.534 --> 02:35.757
(girls scream)

02:35.842 --> 02:37.731
♪ (grunts) Feelings

02:37.815 --> 02:38.867
(girls scream)

02:38.935 --> 02:40.556
I'm gonna put
a stop to this!

02:42.916 --> 02:45.122
(all screaming in fear)

02:50.693 --> 02:52.196
Well, that was
unfortunate.

02:52.263 --> 02:54.370
Hey, what's with all
the cars on the street?

02:54.437 --> 02:56.427
Oh, they're all here
for your surprise party, Meg.

02:56.495 --> 02:58.284
Peter, for God's
sake, you idiot!

02:58.352 --> 03:00.290
We were supposed
to open the door

03:00.359 --> 03:01.895
so everyone could
yell "surprise!"

03:03.535 --> 03:04.973
Surprise!

03:05.024 --> 03:07.598
Oh... Oh, dear.

03:07.666 --> 03:10.425
Mom, if it's a surprise party,
where is everybody?

03:10.492 --> 03:11.796
(hushed):
Chris, what the hell?!

03:11.864 --> 03:13.468
I thought you were
gonna pay the kids

03:13.536 --> 03:15.910
from school to show up!
I gave you $300!

03:15.978 --> 03:17.381
Why do you think
Dad's here?

03:17.449 --> 03:18.787
Hey, Meg, happy birthday.

03:18.854 --> 03:20.676
You're the coolest.

03:20.744 --> 03:23.017
Well, then what are all the cars
doing out there?

03:23.085 --> 03:24.690
Oh, they must be
for Mort's party.

03:24.758 --> 03:26.930
Okay, the first rule
of Jewish fight club

03:26.998 --> 03:30.258
is if somebody says,
"Ow," you stop.

03:30.326 --> 03:31.396
Ow!

03:31.464 --> 03:32.700
Okay, let's eat.

03:32.768 --> 03:34.874
I'm really sorry
about this, honey.

03:34.942 --> 03:36.746
I-It looks like
nobody's coming.

03:36.815 --> 03:39.523
But we had fun at the Teen
Choice Awards, right?

03:39.591 --> 03:40.927
I guess.

03:40.996 --> 03:43.169
Well, I guess we
ought to call it a night.

03:43.237 --> 03:44.673
Come on, Stewie.
Up to bed.

03:44.741 --> 03:48.119
No party? Oh, come on.
I was gonna show a slide show

03:48.187 --> 03:50.058
of all those silly photos
I took of Meg.

03:59.224 --> 04:00.929
Well, happy birthday
anyway, Meg.

04:00.996 --> 04:02.367
See you in the morning.

04:02.435 --> 04:03.705
(doorbell rings)

04:05.277 --> 04:07.066
Hey, Quagmire.
What's going on?

04:07.151 --> 04:08.588
Well, Peter,
a little birdie told me

04:08.656 --> 04:09.642
that today is
Meg's birthday.

04:09.709 --> 04:10.694
You giving me credit?

04:10.747 --> 04:12.133
Yeah, I just told him.

04:12.201 --> 04:13.304
I'm the one
who told him.

04:14.643 --> 04:16.766
So where is
the birthday girl?

04:16.833 --> 04:18.270
Oh, hi, Mr. Quagmire.

04:18.339 --> 04:21.598
Oh, please,
my father is Mr. Quagmi--

04:21.667 --> 04:23.271
Oh, no. He's... Okay,
well, he used

04:23.339 --> 04:24.508
to be Mr. Quagmire.

04:24.577 --> 04:26.615
Now he's, how he's
just Ida Davis.

04:26.684 --> 04:29.057
Anyway, this is a special day
for you, young lady.

04:29.125 --> 04:31.767
Here's a gift for ya.

04:31.834 --> 04:33.004
A scented candle?

04:33.072 --> 04:34.877
As a girl,
I love this!

04:34.944 --> 04:36.784
That was originally $30.

04:36.851 --> 04:38.790
Thanks, Mr. Quagmire.

04:38.858 --> 04:40.362
Well, it's your
18th birthday, Meg.

04:40.430 --> 04:41.700
That's a very important
milestone in

04:41.768 --> 04:42.770
a young girl's...

04:42.838 --> 04:44.576
I mean, a young
woman's life.

04:44.644 --> 04:46.215
Hey, welcome
to the adult club, huh?

04:46.283 --> 04:47.486
And you know what?

04:47.554 --> 04:49.025
You got another member
right next door

04:49.093 --> 04:50.496
if you ever want
to talk and stuff.

04:50.565 --> 04:51.918
Happy birthday.

04:55.632 --> 04:57.537
Hey... Hey, where's
that pinky going, huh?

04:57.604 --> 04:59.410
Where's he going?

04:59.478 --> 05:01.450
Wha, what's he doing?
Get back here.

05:01.518 --> 05:03.055
There you go.

05:03.123 --> 05:05.614
Look at Quagmire hitting
on that skank.

05:05.682 --> 05:07.387
You know he's gonna
close the deal.

05:07.455 --> 05:08.792
Peter, that skank is
your daughter.

05:08.859 --> 05:10.397
Oh, my God,
you're right!

05:10.465 --> 05:12.571
You know, Meg,
I'd love to see you

05:12.639 --> 05:13.925
without your hat on.

05:13.993 --> 05:14.828
Okay.

05:18.846 --> 05:21.220
So, anyway, I'm on approach
into Lambert Field

05:21.288 --> 05:23.862
in some of the worst turbulence
I've ever flown through.

05:23.930 --> 05:25.836
I mean, I have never seen
anything like it.

05:25.904 --> 05:27.943
Everyone in the cabin
was, like, "Aah!"

05:28.028 --> 05:29.582
but I kept my cool.

05:29.650 --> 05:32.091
I trusted my training,
and brought the plane in safely,

05:32.158 --> 05:33.963
and in fact,
it turned out, ironically,

05:34.031 --> 05:36.405
to be one of the smoothest
landings I've ever made.

05:36.473 --> 05:38.545
Well, gosh, Quagmire,
this has been a fun night,

05:38.613 --> 05:40.719
but I guess, uh, you better be
getting home now, huh?

05:40.787 --> 05:42.074
Yeah, it is getting late

05:42.142 --> 05:44.164
I guess I'll go home
and rub out a giggity.

05:44.233 --> 05:45.301
Take it easy, you guys.

05:45.369 --> 05:46.539
See you later, Meg.
(clicks tongue)

05:46.607 --> 05:48.679
Bye.

05:48.747 --> 05:49.717
Okay, that was weird.

05:49.785 --> 05:50.736
That was weird.
Right?

05:50.804 --> 05:52.141
Oh, my God,
so weird.

05:52.210 --> 05:54.031
I tell you something,
if he touches my daughter,

05:54.099 --> 05:55.637
I'm gonna be kicking butts
and taking names!

05:55.704 --> 05:56.808
And then giving
those names

05:56.875 --> 05:58.279
to other people
whose butts I kick.

05:58.346 --> 06:00.202
What's your name?

06:00.270 --> 06:01.339
Derek.

06:01.407 --> 06:03.028
What's your name?

06:03.096 --> 06:03.932
Michael.

06:03.999 --> 06:04.935
You're Derek now!

06:08.414 --> 06:11.122
(phone beeps)

06:15.605 --> 06:16.507
(phone chimes)

06:16.575 --> 06:17.477
Oh! (chuckles)

06:21.524 --> 06:22.896
(phone beeps)

06:28.147 --> 06:29.217
(phone chimes)

06:41.359 --> 06:42.328
(phone chimes)

06:46.208 --> 06:47.445
(phone beeps)

06:56.510 --> 06:57.445
(phone chimes)

07:00.123 --> 07:02.897
Okay, Glenn,
time to reel her in.

07:04.036 --> 07:05.339
(phone beeps)

07:07.948 --> 07:08.918
(phone chimes)

07:10.490 --> 07:13.182
Oh, my God, oh, my God,
oh, my God, oh, my God!

07:15.925 --> 07:17.931
Ah, it's too much, too much.

07:19.137 --> 07:20.540
(phone beeps)

07:22.983 --> 07:24.687
I love stars!

07:27.532 --> 07:30.742
<i>We now return to Grainy Footage
of a Potential Bigfoot</i>

07:30.810 --> 07:33.367
that will surely spark a lively
debate in your household.

07:36.913 --> 07:38.417
Oh, my God!
That is real!

07:38.485 --> 07:40.926
No, total fake.
(all talking at once)

07:40.994 --> 07:42.732
Look at that. That is obviously
a suit. It's a fraud.

07:42.799 --> 07:44.287
Look at the way it walks.
Totally fake.

07:44.355 --> 07:45.692
Why would somebody
make that up, Lois?

07:45.759 --> 07:46.863
What's in it for them?

07:46.930 --> 07:48.435
(knocking)

07:48.503 --> 07:50.341
Oh, hey, Mr. G.
How's it going?

07:50.409 --> 07:51.713
Quagmire, what are you
doing here?

07:51.780 --> 07:53.217
Hi, Glenn.
Bye, you guys.

07:53.285 --> 07:54.689
Me and Glenn
are going out.

07:54.757 --> 07:56.412
What?! Like
hell you are!

07:56.479 --> 07:59.087
Don't worry, Dad!
I'll take care of him!

07:59.155 --> 08:01.379
Stay away from my sis!

08:01.446 --> 08:03.502
Okay, you two have
fun on your date.

08:03.587 --> 08:05.057
What?!
Drive carefully.

08:05.125 --> 08:06.563
We'll see you later.

08:06.630 --> 08:08.035
Lois, are you out
of your mind?!

08:08.102 --> 08:09.907
We can't let Quagmire
take Meg out on a date!

08:09.975 --> 08:11.379
That guy'll bang anything.

08:11.447 --> 08:13.102
Hey, Lois, I'm starving.
What's for dinner?

08:13.169 --> 08:15.292
I made meatloaf.
It's in the fridge.

08:15.360 --> 08:17.283
Hey, Peter, do you mind?

08:17.350 --> 08:18.770
But I have
to get dinner.

08:18.838 --> 08:20.159
Go out!

08:20.227 --> 08:21.162
Peter, nothing's
gonna happen.

08:21.230 --> 08:22.516
Don't you see?

08:22.584 --> 08:24.791
She's only doing this
to get a rise out of us.

08:24.859 --> 08:26.965
If we fight her on it,
she'll only push further.

08:27.033 --> 08:28.904
Well, she may not plan
on sleeping with him,

08:28.973 --> 08:30.728
but you don't know how
smooth Quagmire is, Lois.

08:30.796 --> 08:31.899
He's like a vagician.

08:31.966 --> 08:33.337
Oh, that's clever.

08:33.404 --> 08:35.577
I know! Isn't it?
He practices vagic.

08:35.645 --> 08:37.016
"Vagician" was funnier.

08:37.084 --> 08:38.988
Okay, well, the point is,
we ought to be worried.

08:39.057 --> 08:40.059
Peter, trust me.

08:40.127 --> 08:41.698
I know what's going on
in her head.

08:41.766 --> 08:42.869
It's just a game.

08:42.937 --> 08:45.210
I used to do the same
thing to my parents.

08:45.277 --> 08:46.849
The problem is,
they pushed back,

08:46.916 --> 08:48.756
and the results
were not good.

08:49.927 --> 08:51.063
Mr. Pewterschmidt,

08:51.131 --> 08:52.502
we pumped your
daughter's stomach

08:52.569 --> 08:54.609
and we found vodka, Rohypnol,
a fair amount of DNA

08:54.676 --> 08:56.949
that is not her own
and a class ring.

08:57.017 --> 08:58.087
Harvard?

08:58.155 --> 09:00.361
I think it was
SUNY something.

09:00.430 --> 09:02.000
Oh, I don't want
to hear any more!

09:04.392 --> 09:05.964
So how're
your studies going?

09:06.031 --> 09:07.033
They're going
pretty good.

09:07.101 --> 09:08.606
School's good.

09:08.673 --> 09:10.010
What's your favorite class?

09:10.079 --> 09:11.750
<i>What was your
favorite class?</i>

09:11.818 --> 09:13.589
Okay, let's say it
at the same time

09:13.657 --> 09:14.894
and see if they're
the same.

09:14.961 --> 09:16.499
Okay, one, two, three.

09:16.567 --> 09:17.837
Hist... math!
Math!

09:17.905 --> 09:20.112
Oh, my God, we have
so much in common!

09:20.180 --> 09:21.716
Do you have any brothers
or sisters?

09:21.785 --> 09:22.887
Yeah, I have
two brothers.

09:22.955 --> 09:23.991
Aw, they sound
terrific.

09:24.059 --> 09:25.396
Hey, you want to blow
this joint?

09:25.463 --> 09:26.533
Sure.

09:26.601 --> 09:28.807
Oh, wow, really?!
All right, go for it!

09:28.875 --> 09:30.463
Come on. Let's go.

09:30.531 --> 09:31.868
Oh, oh, you,
you mean leave.

09:31.936 --> 09:33.574
No, yeah, sure.
No, let's go.

09:36.870 --> 09:39.209
Gosh, Meg, I sure had
a swell time with you.

09:39.277 --> 09:41.450
Me, too, Glenn.
God, it's so amazing

09:41.518 --> 09:43.557
that you've been my dad's friend
for, like, years,

09:43.626 --> 09:45.264
and now we have this connection.

09:45.331 --> 09:46.668
Hey, do you want
to come in

09:46.736 --> 09:48.139
for some Crystal Light
or something?

09:48.191 --> 09:50.765
Well, I do believe in me,
but it's getting kind of late.

09:50.833 --> 09:53.274
Um, I really want to
see you again, though.

09:53.342 --> 09:55.180
Oh, you know it.

10:02.991 --> 10:04.528
Oh, God, Peter!

10:04.596 --> 10:05.833
Scared the
hell out of me!

10:05.901 --> 10:08.040
What're you doing here?
I think you know.

10:08.108 --> 10:09.646
Did you have sex
with my daughter?

10:09.714 --> 10:11.686
What? Come on, Peter.

10:11.754 --> 10:13.057
Did you have sex
with my daughter?!

10:13.125 --> 10:14.863
Peter, trust me,
it's not happening.

10:14.931 --> 10:16.369
(sighs)
All right. Good.

10:16.436 --> 10:18.174
Yeah, she's really making
me work for it.

10:18.242 --> 10:19.646
Maybe you could
talk to her.

10:19.714 --> 10:21.018
Well, I'll try,

10:21.085 --> 10:23.125
but sometimes she can be
as stubborn as a mule.

10:23.192 --> 10:24.797
I tell you, you tell her
to do something once,

10:24.865 --> 10:26.369
she does the opposite.

10:26.437 --> 10:27.907
You know, it's like
she ain't even heard you

10:27.975 --> 10:29.178
in the first place.

10:29.246 --> 10:30.550
It's like talking
to a brick wall.

10:30.618 --> 10:32.222
Worse than talking...

10:32.290 --> 10:34.112
Even a brick wall doesn't tell
you they understand you,

10:34.179 --> 10:35.516
and then go do the opposite,
you know?

10:35.585 --> 10:37.072
So it's no surprise to me

10:37.139 --> 10:38.359
that you're having
these difficulties.

10:38.427 --> 10:41.302
That-that just seems
to be the way she is.

10:41.370 --> 10:43.176
You know, whether it's just
that she's not listening

10:43.260 --> 10:45.701
or whether it's that she's
making a conscious decision

10:45.769 --> 10:48.778
to defy your wishes,
who can say, you know?

10:48.846 --> 10:50.450
And I would say,
in some respects,

10:50.518 --> 10:52.825
having a strong-willed kid
is a good thing,

10:52.893 --> 10:54.866
but it can get frustrating
as hell on the other side.

10:54.933 --> 10:56.137
So, you know, lieve me,

10:56.204 --> 10:57.608
I hear loud and clear
where you're--

10:57.675 --> 10:59.916
Wait a second!
No, I won't talk to her!

10:59.984 --> 11:02.223
And I want you to stay the hell
away from her!

11:02.291 --> 11:04.297
Peter it's me-- Quagmire.

11:04.365 --> 11:05.903
This is what I do.

11:05.970 --> 11:08.578
Besides, Meg is 18 now
and you've gotta let go.

11:08.646 --> 11:10.618
You've done your job.
It's my turn now.

11:10.686 --> 11:12.825
Look, Quagmire, you're
one of my best pals,

11:12.894 --> 11:15.000
and I'm asking you
not to do this.

11:15.068 --> 11:16.940
I want to help you,
Peter, I really do,

11:17.007 --> 11:19.281
but it's-- it's like you're
asking a fish not to swim.

11:19.349 --> 11:20.669
She's legal and I'm going in.

11:20.737 --> 11:22.241
Well, we'll see about that.

11:22.309 --> 11:24.047
I ain't afraid
to stand up to friends.

11:24.115 --> 11:25.335
Just ask Spartacus.

11:25.402 --> 11:26.873
I'm Spartacus.

11:26.941 --> 11:28.429
I'm Spartacus.

11:28.497 --> 11:29.465
That guy's
Spartacus.

11:32.844 --> 11:36.656
<i>ANNOUNCER: We now return to Two Lame
Chicks on Vacation in Mexico.</i>

11:37.928 --> 11:40.587
Oh, my God, don't
drink the water.

11:40.655 --> 11:42.961
I'm so going to brush
my teeth with tequila.

11:43.029 --> 11:44.700
Mexico!
Mexico!

11:44.752 --> 11:46.540
Hey, is this beach topless?

11:46.591 --> 11:48.965
No, but my
margarita's bottomless.

11:49.033 --> 11:50.637
Mexico!
Mexico!

11:50.705 --> 11:53.781
That cute guy's been
staring at you all night.

11:53.849 --> 11:57.327
Oh, my God. I'm going to go poo
now, so I don't have to later.

11:57.395 --> 11:59.166
Mexico!
Mexico!

11:59.234 --> 12:02.059
Hey, you want to see
my pictures from Mexico?

12:02.127 --> 12:06.675
Look, Janine, I just-- this is--
I can't with you anymore.

12:06.743 --> 12:09.150
It's all the time.
This is a job.

12:09.218 --> 12:10.856
Please take off
that silly hat.

12:10.923 --> 12:12.996
(phone ringing)

12:13.064 --> 12:16.675
GIRL: Mexico!
I... I can't talk right now.

12:19.502 --> 12:20.371
You okay?

12:20.456 --> 12:21.759
Yeah, babe.

12:21.827 --> 12:23.415
I got to pee,
but I don't want to move.

12:23.483 --> 12:25.020
I'm so comfortable right now.

12:25.105 --> 12:26.358
I can pause it.

12:26.443 --> 12:27.662
I guess you could
pause it...

12:27.730 --> 12:29.016
but you can't pause me!

12:29.068 --> 12:30.456
Fast forward.
Fast forward.

12:30.523 --> 12:31.910
Fast forward.
Glenn, stop.

12:31.994 --> 12:33.365
I can't breathe.
I can't breathe either.

12:33.416 --> 12:34.535
This is torture
for me, too.

12:34.586 --> 12:35.539
No fair. Stop.

12:35.590 --> 12:37.195
I'm going to...
(farts)

12:37.263 --> 12:38.834
Sorry.

12:38.902 --> 12:40.941
Ah, that's all right.
It's just your body.

12:41.009 --> 12:42.613
Sometimes things slip out.

12:42.681 --> 12:44.151
Probably just making
room for something.

12:44.219 --> 12:45.757
Like what?

12:45.841 --> 12:48.199
Hey, gang, got room for one more
right in the middle of you two?

12:48.266 --> 12:50.206
Come on, scooch apart, there.

12:50.273 --> 12:52.145
Ooh, what's this?
Quagmire's cell phone?

12:52.230 --> 12:53.817
Well, now that you're with Meg,

12:53.903 --> 12:56.627
you don't need to be talking to,
uh, "Backbush" anymore.

12:56.711 --> 12:59.052
Oh, and I'll send a text to
"Possible Nipple Ring"

12:59.120 --> 13:00.591
saying you're off the market.

13:00.659 --> 13:02.145
(phone beeps)

13:02.213 --> 13:04.487
You're "Possible Nipple Ring"?

13:04.572 --> 13:06.728
All right, well, I better
send a text to "Backbush."

13:06.795 --> 13:07.932
(buzzing)

13:08.000 --> 13:09.303
Oh, come on.
I'm "Backbush"?

13:09.371 --> 13:11.009
This can't be a
surprise to you, Peter.

13:11.077 --> 13:12.648
Yeah, I knew.

13:12.715 --> 13:14.973
(sobbing):
I just didn't know you knew.

13:17.014 --> 13:18.619
Okay, what compound is this?

13:18.686 --> 13:20.023
That's sodium chloride.

13:20.074 --> 13:21.595
That's right.
How about this one?

13:21.663 --> 13:22.933
Hydrogen peroxide.

13:23.001 --> 13:24.990
God, you're so smart.
How about this one?

13:25.058 --> 13:28.050
QM2? I'm not sure
what that is.

13:28.118 --> 13:29.622
It's Quag-megium.

13:29.690 --> 13:31.528
It's the strongest
compound on Earth.

13:31.596 --> 13:32.933
Nothing can separate it.

13:33.001 --> 13:35.241
It has an atomic weight
of awesome.

13:35.308 --> 13:37.214
You're such a
cutie patootie.

13:37.282 --> 13:40.191
If I'm a cutie patootie, then
you're a peenie-vageenie.

13:40.259 --> 13:41.312
Aww!

13:41.396 --> 13:43.770
I heard a cute "aw" in there.
Cool down!

13:48.570 --> 13:51.329
Meg, there's something
we need to talk about.

13:51.397 --> 13:53.838
Dad, I swear to God, I thought
you could flush those things.

13:53.905 --> 13:55.330
Meg, you ever heard
of Joan Van Ark?

13:55.355 --> 13:56.413
No.

13:56.414 --> 13:57.984
Here's a picture
of Joan Van Ark.

13:58.053 --> 13:59.824
Oh, my God, she's gorgeous.

13:59.892 --> 14:01.129
Gorgeous. Yes.

14:01.196 --> 14:02.901
Yes, Meg, gorgeous.

14:02.969 --> 14:04.673
Yes.
Every man wanted her.

14:04.742 --> 14:06.580
But one man got her.

14:06.648 --> 14:09.858
A man she trusted to keep her
safe and beautiful forever.

14:09.926 --> 14:11.430
That man was Glenn Quagmire.

14:11.498 --> 14:13.035
And two short months later,

14:13.103 --> 14:14.975
this is what happened
to Joan Van Ark.

14:15.043 --> 14:17.517
Oh! Oh, my God!

14:17.585 --> 14:19.390
I don't want this
to happen to you, Meg.

14:19.458 --> 14:21.598
I don't want you to turn
into a hilarious photograph.

14:21.666 --> 14:23.237
Dad, I know what
you're trying to do,

14:23.305 --> 14:24.775
and I want you
to stop it.

14:24.844 --> 14:25.745
Mom!

14:25.813 --> 14:26.882
What is it, Meg?

14:26.951 --> 14:28.755
Mom, tell Dad
to leave me alone.

14:28.823 --> 14:31.029
I'm 18, and he keeps
treating me like a kid.

14:31.097 --> 14:34.542
Peter, I told you not to push
her about this Quagmire thing.

14:34.610 --> 14:36.009
If you push too hard,

14:36.034 --> 14:37.638
you're going to push her
right into his arms.

14:37.720 --> 14:38.973
Well, what am I supposed to do?

14:39.041 --> 14:40.194
Nothing.

14:40.262 --> 14:41.766
This is a big game
Meg is playing,

14:41.834 --> 14:44.073
and the only way to win
is not to play it.

14:44.142 --> 14:46.615
<i>Is that a WarGames reference?
Might be.</i>

14:46.684 --> 14:49.024
<i>You know WarGames?
Yeah.</i>

14:49.091 --> 14:50.596
Still finding out
new stuff about you.

14:50.664 --> 14:51.767
That's the adventure.

14:51.834 --> 14:52.971
There's a nerd in there.

14:53.039 --> 14:54.107
Maybe there is.

14:54.175 --> 14:55.546
I might bang her later.

14:55.614 --> 14:56.984
How about a nice
game of chess?

14:57.052 --> 14:58.155
I prefer banging.

14:58.206 --> 15:00.162
Dad, have you seen my book bag?

15:00.229 --> 15:01.834
What, Chris?
(screaming)

15:06.049 --> 15:07.453
Oh, Peter, there you are.

15:07.520 --> 15:09.626
Would you go tell Meg
that lunch is on the table?

15:09.695 --> 15:11.400
Oh, Meg's not here.
What do you mean?

15:11.468 --> 15:13.172
She and Quagmire went up
to his cabin for the weekend.

15:13.174 --> 15:13.854
What?!

15:13.858 --> 15:15.530
Yeah, I drew you
a crude flip book

15:15.598 --> 15:16.868
to explain what's happening.

15:22.405 --> 15:24.043
Okay, I got
a little off track there,

15:24.110 --> 15:25.580
but they went to his cabin.

15:25.632 --> 15:28.140
Peter, Quagmire has
a name for that cabin.

15:28.208 --> 15:29.811
He calls it his sex cabin.

15:29.880 --> 15:31.885
No, he doesn't.
He calls it "The Stuffet Inn."

15:31.954 --> 15:33.658
Oh, my God, I can't believe
you knew about this

15:33.726 --> 15:34.812
and you let her go.

15:34.880 --> 15:36.150
Hey, don't give me that crap.

15:36.218 --> 15:37.923
I'm doing exactly
what you told me to do.

15:37.990 --> 15:39.880
You said don't mess with her
business, so I didn't.

15:39.947 --> 15:42.070
Peter, this is different.

15:42.138 --> 15:44.679
It's one thing to
rebelliously flaunt an older guy

15:44.746 --> 15:46.986
in front of your parents,
but it's a whole other thing

15:47.055 --> 15:49.495
to go away with him for the
weekend to his sex cabin.

15:49.563 --> 15:51.235
Oh, is that right?

15:51.302 --> 15:54.813
Oh, don't worry, Peter, he's
not going to sleep with her.

15:54.881 --> 15:57.121
That's you. Nerd.

15:57.189 --> 16:00.331
Look, everyone knows if you go
away with a guy for the weekend

16:00.399 --> 16:02.740
and don't have sex with him,
you're a huge bitch.

16:02.807 --> 16:04.212
We got to stop them.

16:04.280 --> 16:05.716
So you admit you were wrong.
Yes.

16:05.784 --> 16:07.757
You admit you were stupid.
Yes, yes.

16:07.824 --> 16:09.647
You admit all women are stupid.
No.

16:09.731 --> 16:11.353
All right, I'll take
what I can get.

16:11.420 --> 16:12.522
Come on.
To the Peter-dactyl.

16:14.264 --> 16:16.871
(screeching)

16:18.728 --> 16:20.098
(buzzing, crackling)

16:21.588 --> 16:24.530
Oh, no, now I got
to take care of the babies.

16:35.303 --> 16:37.226
Look, Peter,
his car's still there.

16:37.227 --> 16:38.765
Maybe they haven't left yet.

16:38.832 --> 16:41.943
Quagmire, let me in,
you son of a bitch.

16:42.010 --> 16:44.050
QUAGMIRE (recorded): I'm sorry
I'm not home to receive you.

16:44.118 --> 16:46.224
The reason being that you have
sufficiently scared me away

16:46.291 --> 16:47.929
from your wife or daughter.

16:47.997 --> 16:51.541
I plan to get help and use
better judgment in the future.

16:51.610 --> 16:53.080
Wait a minute, so Quagmire

16:53.148 --> 16:54.719
just changed all of a
sudden, just like that?

16:54.787 --> 16:56.123
You want me to read this or not?

16:56.192 --> 16:57.897
No, Grandpa, I don't.

16:57.964 --> 17:00.004
No kid wants to be read
anything any more.

17:00.071 --> 17:02.411
Computers exist.
It's just you won't leave.

17:02.480 --> 17:05.321
Okay, where were we?
Quagmire's front door.

17:05.390 --> 17:06.926
You think they're
hiding in there?

17:06.978 --> 17:09.151
(engine revving)
Oh, no! Peter, look.

17:09.236 --> 17:11.208
See you later, suckers.

17:14.270 --> 17:16.727
Oh, good luck to them.
Peter!

17:16.795 --> 17:17.747
Oh, right, right.
Let's go.

17:20.440 --> 17:21.928
(tires squealing)

17:23.316 --> 17:25.189
(horns honking)

17:26.728 --> 17:29.252
We're never going
to get up there.

17:29.321 --> 17:31.175
I wonder what's causing
all this traffic.

17:31.243 --> 17:32.948
Oh, boy.
Yep, there's the problem.

17:33.016 --> 17:34.052
Not drawn yet.

17:37.464 --> 17:39.269
Come on, guys.
Really? Let's go.

17:39.337 --> 17:41.076
What the hell's
going on up there?

17:41.144 --> 17:42.982
(snoring)

17:44.388 --> 17:46.912
What...? Yep. Yep.

17:48.285 --> 17:50.257
(owl hooting)

17:52.632 --> 17:53.935
So tell the truth.

17:54.003 --> 17:55.976
Have you brought
other women up here before?

17:56.044 --> 17:58.251
Honestly? Two.
Really?

17:58.319 --> 18:01.161
Yep, I brought the ashes
of my third grade teacher,

18:01.228 --> 18:02.799
Mrs. Nicholson, and spread
them across the lake,

18:02.867 --> 18:04.171
per her last request.

18:04.238 --> 18:05.240
Oh.

18:05.308 --> 18:06.713
The other was some skag

18:06.780 --> 18:08.046
I met on a dock
four miles from here.

18:08.071 --> 18:09.174
What?!

18:09.205 --> 18:11.746
(imitates buzzer)
Strike four, Jelly Jealouson.

18:11.814 --> 18:13.134
The other was my sister.

18:13.202 --> 18:15.224
(both laughing)

18:15.292 --> 18:17.465
(sighs)
It's so nice up here.

18:17.534 --> 18:19.505
I know.
I love the way the fire

18:19.573 --> 18:21.830
makes the shadows dance around
behind us.

18:21.898 --> 18:24.004
One time, my friends
and I went camping,

18:24.072 --> 18:26.278
and nobody could
start a campfire,

18:26.347 --> 18:29.256
and then I tried to start
the campfire, and I could.

18:29.323 --> 18:30.794
That's insane.

18:30.861 --> 18:32.399
Wha-- what is going on
over here?

18:32.467 --> 18:34.406
Wha-- are we taking
our shirts off now?

18:34.474 --> 18:35.727
Okay, follow the leader.

18:37.752 --> 18:39.673
Come on, Peter, hurry!

18:39.742 --> 18:40.911
Wait wait,
hold on, hold on, hold on.

18:40.980 --> 18:42.450
(loon calling)

18:42.518 --> 18:44.357
Listen to that.
It's a loon.

18:44.424 --> 18:45.895
That's beautiful.

18:45.962 --> 18:48.236
You know, we ought to get
a (bleep) cabin up here.

18:48.304 --> 18:50.343
Peter, we're wasting time.

18:50.411 --> 18:53.085
Quagmire's in there about to
have sex with our daughter.

18:53.154 --> 18:54.373
That son of a bitch.

18:54.442 --> 18:57.752
Let's-- wait-- w-wait
a minute, do you hear that?

18:57.820 --> 18:59.156
I don't hear anything.

18:59.224 --> 19:01.264
I know.
Isn't it bliss?

19:01.331 --> 19:02.668
Peter, let's go!

19:02.736 --> 19:05.344
Mm. Thanks for
the ice cream, Glenn.

19:05.412 --> 19:06.782
And you're right, somehow

19:06.850 --> 19:08.254
it does taste better
in my underpants.

19:08.322 --> 19:10.027
Yeah, it's like being
at the beach, huh?

19:10.094 --> 19:12.167
Now get over here while
the inside of your mouth

19:12.235 --> 19:13.739
is still freezing cold.

19:15.379 --> 19:17.752
There you are,
you son of a bitch!

19:19.727 --> 19:21.650
You get away from
my daughter, you pervert!

19:21.717 --> 19:23.054
Meg, get in the car,
we're going home.

19:23.122 --> 19:24.676
I'm not going home!

19:24.744 --> 19:27.234
I'm 18, and you can't tell
me what to do anymore.

19:27.286 --> 19:29.041
Meg, I'm only going
to say this once.

19:29.108 --> 19:31.214
You may be an adult,
but you're still my daughter,

19:31.283 --> 19:33.355
and it's my job to protect
you from errant wieners.

19:33.424 --> 19:35.062
So, I don't care
how old you are,

19:35.129 --> 19:37.603
you're going to do what I say
and get in the damn car!

19:37.671 --> 19:39.643
Yes, Daddy.

19:43.591 --> 19:47.018
If you ever touch
my daughter again,

19:47.086 --> 19:49.285
I will cut your thing off
and feed it to Brian.

19:49.311 --> 19:50.513
Okay.

19:50.632 --> 19:52.871
And Peter and I get this cabin
for one weekend a month.

19:52.939 --> 19:53.841
Do you understand me?

19:53.910 --> 19:55.079
Yes, ma'am.

19:55.146 --> 19:57.303
Peter, I got us the cabin.
Yay.

19:57.371 --> 19:59.309
I don't want to see your
face knocking on our door

19:59.378 --> 20:01.116
for at least a month.

20:01.184 --> 20:04.226
Would you sign the
guest book on your way out?

20:04.294 --> 20:06.986
Lois... Griffin.

20:07.054 --> 20:09.377
Peter... Griffin.

20:09.446 --> 20:12.320
We... heard... a loon.

20:15.767 --> 20:18.776
You know, Mom and Dad, I'm
really glad that you kept me

20:18.844 --> 20:20.448
from doing what
I was going to do.

20:20.516 --> 20:22.287
Well, that's what
parents are for, Meg.

20:22.355 --> 20:23.993
No matter what age you are.

20:24.061 --> 20:26.936
We love you and we just
never want to see you hurt.

20:27.004 --> 20:29.010
I only wish I'd seen
what was going on

20:29.078 --> 20:30.516
from the start,
like your father did.

20:30.583 --> 20:32.840
Well, I know the signs...

20:32.925 --> 20:34.963
because the same thing
happened to me.

20:35.015 --> 20:35.817
An older neighbor.

20:35.902 --> 20:37.974
Her name was Elaine.

20:38.025 --> 20:41.151
I was 18 and my body was firm
from push-ups and sit-ups.

20:41.202 --> 20:43.292
I was stunning.

20:43.359 --> 20:44.630
But while my body was mature,

20:44.698 --> 20:46.837
I had the mind of a 12-year-old.

20:46.905 --> 20:50.014
Elaine invited me over
with the promise of pie.

20:50.083 --> 20:51.754
Little did I know
this would lead

20:51.822 --> 20:54.831
to an eight-year-long
psychosexual entanglement.

20:54.899 --> 20:56.637
She's probably dead now.

20:56.705 --> 20:59.012
Life's funny sometimes.

20:59.080 --> 21:00.901
And... scene.

21:00.902 --> 22:01.902
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru